,title,link,text,language,family
0,El Molo people - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Molo_people,"The El Molo, also known as Elmolo, Dehes, Fura-Pawa and Ldes, are an ethnic group mainly inhabiting the northern Eastern Province of Kenya. They historically spoke the El Molo language as a mother tongue, an Afro-Asiatic language of the Cushitic branch; currently, most El Molo speak Samburu.",El Molo,Afro-Asiatic
1,El Molo language - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Molo_language,"El Molo (sometimes spelled Elmolo) is a moribund or extinct language belonging to the Cushitic branch of the Afro-Asiatic language family. It was spoken by the El Molo people on the southeastern shore of Lake Turkana, in northern Kenya.",El Molo,Afro-Asiatic
