7,The El Molo Community of Kenya — Google Arts & Culture,https://artsandculture.google.com/story/the-el-molo-community-of-kenya-national-museums-of-kenya/JwWhe7Y5wdpmKQ?hl=en,"The El Molo belong to the Cushitic linguistic group and are today nearly extinct. The El Molo historically spoke the El Molo language, which is regarded as endangered by UNESCO. In 2008, the National Museums of Kenya established the Desert Museum in Loiyangalani, to preserve and promote the unique cultures of the eight communities living around Lake Turkana region, namely: El Molo, Turkana ...",El Molo,Afro-Asiatic
